@startuml
actor Administrator
participant "Word card" as UI
participant "Admin gateway" as Gateway
participant "Core" as Core
participant "GotIt Backend" as Backend
database "product_gotit" as DB
participant "Pixabay or GPT image API" as Provider
Administrator -> UI: Search/filter every user's words
UI -> Gateway: GET words and cached images
Gateway -> Core: Authenticate verified administrator
Gateway -> Backend: Fixed allowlisted read
Backend -> DB: Scoped metadata and current cached bytes
Backend --> UI: Cards with inline image actions
opt Choose Pixabay
  Administrator -> UI: Open gallery in the card
  UI -> Gateway: GET words/:id/stock-images (q, page)
  Gateway -> Backend: Fixed scoped gallery route
  Backend -> DB: Verify scoped word exists
  Backend -> Provider: Cached public image search (24 hours)
  Backend --> UI: Previews, attribution and signed selections
end
Administrator -> UI: Select thumbnail or click GPT (optional prompt)
UI -> Gateway: words image action (operationId, item/concept revisions)
Gateway -> Core: Require content.write and MFA
Gateway -> Backend: Fixed words/:id/image route
Backend -> Core: Independently require permission and MFA
Backend -> DB: Durable preparation; derive exact image identity if absent
note right: Preserve current item/catalog bytes; no manual setup screen
Backend -> DB: Stable child receipt + reserved image revision
Backend -> Provider: Exact signed photo download or GPT prompt
alt Valid provider result and unchanged item and meaning
  Backend -> DB: Transaction: lock item and concept, validate claim, store image
  note right: Advance shared image pointer and revision; publish audit
  Backend --> UI: Stable success receipt
  UI -> Gateway: Refresh cards and cached images
else Provider unavailable or stale item/meaning
  Backend -> DB: Release claim; retain current image
  Backend --> UI: Failure/conflict; preserve retry UUID and payload
end
@enduml